From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Sep 2026 15:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/lima: pin runtime PM on S5P6818 (GPU resume wedges the SoC)

The Mali-400 comes up fine from the bootloader power-up, but the first
runtime-PM suspend/resume cycle hard-wedges the whole SoC: lima idles the
GPU (200 ms autosuspend), and the reset-deassert + GPU re-init on the next
resume hangs the interconnect (LED heartbeat stops = total wedge). It is
reproducible with a bare `echo on > .../c0070000.gpu/power/control`, and it
is what makes any compositor (GNOME/mutter idles->suspends->resumes the GPU
every frame) hang. The clock is not the cause - the VR clock reads enabled
across the wedge - so this is the boot blob's GPU clock/reset handoff not
being re-entrant, which a from-scratch mainline bring-up cannot fix from the
kernel side.

Pin a runtime-PM reference on this SoC so the GPU stays in its known-good
boot state and never suspend/resume-cycles. The GPU clock stays on and Lima
GLES2 keeps working; only runtime power-gating of the GPU is given up. Gated
on the S5P6818 machine compatible so other Lima platforms are unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_drv.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_drv.c
index 9a0eb1092..e6a8cee2a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_drv.c
@@ -420,6 +420,18 @@ static int lima_pdev_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	pm_runtime_use_autosuspend(ldev->dev);
 	pm_runtime_enable(ldev->dev);
 
+	/*
+	 * S5P6818: a runtime-PM suspend/resume cycle hard-wedges the SoC (the
+	 * reset-deassert + GPU re-init on resume hangs the interconnect; the boot
+	 * blob's GPU clock/reset handoff is not re-entrant, and forcing a resume
+	 * via power/control=on reproduces the wedge every time). Pin a runtime-PM
+	 * reference on this SoC so the GPU stays in its known-good boot state and
+	 * never suspend/resume-cycles - the clock stays on and GLES2 keeps
+	 * working, only runtime power-gating of the GPU is given up.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("nexell,s5p6818"))
+		pm_runtime_get_sync(ldev->dev);
+
 	/*
 	 * Register the DRM device with the core and the connectors with
 	 * sysfs.

